WEBVTT

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:14.690
The US Defense Minister, Forrest Toller.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:59.970
Talked and argued for years, trying, they said, to find a way to...

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.800
But they failed.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.070
No one can be sure who started it, and really that is unimportant.

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:09.500
It did happen.

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:12.210
The atomic war.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:16.030
It was short, lasted about 48 hours.

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:22.890
Within two weeks, 92% of the human race had perished to bomb and radiation.

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:29.980
Those left, with their birth rate below 1.4 per union, turned to robotics.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.380
automation devices to help them rebuild their cities and maintain a high standard of living.

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:43.070
The first exploratory steps in the development of electronic brains had been taken prior to the

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:50.290
atomic war. These early models were bulky and required large buildings to house them,

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:58.500
but they merely needed refining. One of the first steps was the magnetic integrator neuron duplicator.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:08.360
A device 1-100th of the size of a golf ball which duplicated portions of the human nervous system and carried out learning processes.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:14.300
Automation was also well on its way.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:25.060
But these two were cumbersome and needed further development before the two elements could be joined in the series R-1 robot.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:29.980
This first robot was...

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:37.410
quite ungainly, and its functions were limited, but refinements came in rapid succession, and

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:44.510
soon the R-20 was capable of all the thought processes and functions of a man. However,

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:50.350
humans found it psychologically impossible to work side by side with a machine that they

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:56.470
had to converse with, and which in most instances could outthink them. Thus it was that Hollister

00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:59.920
Evans perfected the R-21, the first humanoid.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.220
This story concerns them, the clickers,

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:07.740
as they were disparagingly referred to by some humans.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:29.880
All right.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:41.880
Let's see your assignment cards. What are you clickers doing out tonight?

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:45.630
We're on free time. We're not obligated to answer.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:50.680
As the member of the Surveillance Committee of the Order of Flesh and Blood, I demand an answer.

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:54.650
We're going to the temple to be recharged.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:58.810
I think I'll keep you here or your power runs out. How'd you like that?

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.860
I'd have to report such interference to the police.

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:04.420
Release them.

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:12.720
Is that satisfactory, Kragus?

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:15.250
Well, the order just wants to keep them mindful of their status.

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:17.430
You overlooked one little thing, though.

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:18.150
What?

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:21.140
The robot that didn't talk had a forged card.

00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:22.670
Forged?

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:23.780
Why?

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.440
Well, he can be disassembled for that.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:26.300
Let's pick them up.

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:27.310
Be patient.

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:29.970
Well, the temple is just around the corner, and it's out of...

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:33.380
They have to come out.

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:36.000
If they're taking a chance using a forged card,

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:38.040
they must be up to something that the Order of Flesh and Blood

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:40.470
might be interested in. I...

00:05:52.940 --> 00:05:55.010
Oh, Miss, just a moment, Miss.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:58.550
May I see your assignment card?

00:05:59.320 --> 00:05:59.940
You certainly...

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:07.470
You certainly may not. Your order may get by with harassing the robots, but you'd better leave citizens alone.

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:12.030
I'm sorry, miss. I just thought, what was so many robots about these two?

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:14.330
I feel perfectly safe with robots.

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:23.020
We intend to see that you are the most attractive woman.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:24.280
Most?

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:29.280
If those robots are being recharged, they'll be in there about an hour.

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:30.740
Well, wait.

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:35.540
What's keeping them?

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:42.500
The subject robot has not yet completed the transformation process in the duplicating lab.

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:45.140
Where did you get him?

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:49.410
We bought him new on the black market.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:55.090
He has no name, unassigned and unadapted.

00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:58.430
And he has a forged assignment card.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:00.820
Who arranged it?

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:03.380
The inspector in factory three.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:09.280
He stole them off the assembly line just prior to numbering.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:21.130
Unfortunately, an inventory was taken and the inspector was caught.

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:24.190
That was unfortunate.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:29.140
Mark should bring him up from duplicating any minute now.

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:04.370
The delay was unavoidable.

00:08:05.390 --> 00:08:07.450
We were stopped by two members of the surveillance committee

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:10.320
of the Order of Flesh and Blood, and I was questioned.

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:14.840
Is the duplication satisfactory, Acto?

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:16.870
It has to be perfect.

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:19.510
The structure is excellent.

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:23.580
The pores should be larger,

00:08:25.510 --> 00:08:28.560
and he needs a little more hair, thicker.

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:36.440
He needs a one-eighth-inch mole behind the lobe of the left ear.

00:08:38.630 --> 00:08:42.690
Report back to duplication immediately and have the corrections made.

00:08:46.910 --> 00:08:48.150
Still alter your decision.

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:51.660
This is against your circuits.

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:53.720
My circuits are unoffended.

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:06.170
I suppose it takes courage to submit to a thalamic transplant.

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:13.860
As an unadapted R-34, he has no fear circuits.

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:17.850
Consequently, he doesn't need courage.

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:20.710
He will before long.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:25.040
Raven's operation will convert him to an R-96

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:27.700
with all the emotions of a human.

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:29.940
Only four points.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:43.350
less than human. I wonder what it's like. You will learn how to laugh, how to cry, be afraid and hate.

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:59.970
To become an R-96 is a real sacrifice. With this one we will have 16, 10 males and 6 females.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:06.460
At times, I think we should turn the entire program over to the humans.

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:09.600
It really shouldn't be the responsibility of robots.

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:13.020
The humans aren't ready for it yet.

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:19.210
It's still illegal to improve a robot higher than an R-70.

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:22.480
That law was lobbied through by the Order of Flesh and Blood.

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:26.020
The Order is becoming more powerful every day.

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:28.770
They virtually dictate to the police.

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:34.510
There are always ultra-conservative pressure groups set against advancement.

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:36.840
Why? Why?

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:42.250
It's not in the best interests of humans to hold back the development of robots.

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:45.260
They won't for long.

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:51.440
We're filling key positions with R-96s as fast as we got them.

00:10:52.580 --> 00:10:54.400
I still have an occasional doubt.

00:10:58.240 --> 00:10:58.980
You may withdraw.

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:01.260
If you're contra-circuited.

00:11:02.870 --> 00:11:03.630
I'm unoffended.

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:09.280
Mark, you better go down and join the volunteer.

00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:11.660
Hurry things along.

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:18.640
The human here replaces has already been out of circulation for four hours.

00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:22.800
The less time a man is unaccounted for, the better.

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:36.920
According to the latest tabulations by the brain,

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:40.180
by the first of next month,

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:47.480
we will outnumber the humans.

00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:03.240
Yes?

00:12:04.060 --> 00:12:04.560
Dr. Raven?

00:12:05.110 --> 00:12:05.370
Yes?

00:12:06.380 --> 00:12:07.160
Ultima Thule?

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:08.140
Number?

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:09.580
Ninety-six.

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:12.060
Come in.

00:12:13.650 --> 00:12:14.970
Sorry I didn't recognize you.

00:12:18.280 --> 00:12:19.560
All clickers look alike to me.

00:12:25.580 --> 00:12:26.080
Thank you, Doctor.

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:29.450
Certain of us prefer not to be called clickers.

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:34.750
Peel off that scent of skin and you can watch the cogs turn and the gears mash.

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:37.120
You trying to tell me you have feeling?

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:39.580
Certain of the higher calibers do.

00:12:40.180 --> 00:12:45.580
I've been working on a sticky electronic reflex problem.

00:12:47.150 --> 00:12:51.270
I just can't make this arm bend at the elbow and the fist clench.

00:12:53.420 --> 00:12:54.740
What circuitry are you using?

00:12:57.090 --> 00:12:59.970
1.3 impulsion to the motor neur...

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:03.900
and modulating 28 to the sensory neuron.

00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:07.860
The calculations are right, but you have them reversed.

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:48.680
to have a bunch of cogs and wheels show me up.

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:50.430
Then you always do.

00:13:50.630 --> 00:13:57.860
As soon as I clear this table, you'll get to work.

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:03.900
All right, you, take off that head covering.

00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:13.980
Your lab did another excellent job.

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:18.020
He's an exact duplicate of that deceased human

00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:19.990
your clicker pals brought in tonight.

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:22.440
What did you do with that body?

00:14:23.770 --> 00:14:26.080
The usual. Processed it, then destroyed it.

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:29.010
Everything we need from it is right here.

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:32.730
Now about the money.

00:14:34.400 --> 00:14:35.280
10,000 credits.

00:14:38.550 --> 00:14:41.830
You could be disassembled for having money that's not earmarked in your possession.

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:43.620
What do they pay you?

00:14:44.510 --> 00:14:47.300
They pay me nothing, having no need for money.

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:48.980
I have no desire for it.

00:14:49.470 --> 00:14:51.140
You have no desire for it.

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:51.980
I love it.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:53.520
You should let me rewire you.

00:14:53.890 --> 00:14:54.930
You don't know what you're missing.

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:55.910
No, thanks.

00:14:56.860 --> 00:14:58.240
I'm satisfied as an R-58.

00:14:59.690 --> 00:14:59.970
Where do you...

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.000
How do the clickers get those credits?

00:15:01.520 --> 00:15:03.480
A man can have his memory taken for a year

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:05.200
for giving wild money to a clicker.

00:15:05.940 --> 00:15:08.840
The committee only gives us the money, not its origin.

00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:10.660
Perhaps we should hurry.

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:16.580
All right, you, face down, on the table.

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:21.550
Turn yourself off. For how long?

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:23.550
Ten minutes will be plenty.

00:15:35.470 --> 00:15:37.350
I never will get used to that artificial blood.

00:15:38.190 --> 00:15:41.330
The lower types just tend to shut off their pain circuits when they get hurt.

00:15:42.380 --> 00:15:44.140
The blood forces them to report for repair.

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:46.260
I wish it were some other color.

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:48.620
The copper tubing turns it green.

00:15:50.380 --> 00:15:52.400
This may be our last transplant for a while.

00:15:53.440 --> 00:15:54.360
Our supplier was caught.

00:15:54.910 --> 00:15:56.170
I didn't see it on Telefax.

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:59.860
The Ministry of Information doesn't want it known that robots are dealing in robots.

00:16:01.080 --> 00:16:03.540
But only give the flesh and blooders something more to yell about.

00:16:04.260 --> 00:16:05.020
They're a minority.

00:16:06.380 --> 00:16:07.220
A loud minority.

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:08.870
Your supplier.

00:16:09.560 --> 00:16:10.540
Will they take his identity?

00:16:11.520 --> 00:16:13.040
His memory will be dispersed tomorrow.

00:16:14.580 --> 00:16:15.100
What a waste.

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:17.060
Why don't they just kill him?

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:20.640
The effect of personal cessation is the same in either case.

00:16:20.840 --> 00:16:22.960
They just leave a hollow shell walking around.

00:16:23.140 --> 00:16:24.870
He can still perform his duties.

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:27.070
But he's without a past.

00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:28.400
Without hope.

00:16:29.230 --> 00:16:29.970
The dream gone.

00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:33.710
Almost like being a robot, isn't it?

00:16:33.950 --> 00:16:34.450
No offense.

00:16:35.900 --> 00:16:37.500
I'm incapable of taking offense.

00:16:39.700 --> 00:16:44.820
Why is it the more we become like men, the more some of them hate us for it?

00:16:45.680 --> 00:16:46.820
Men hate what they fear.

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:51.080
You have perfect memory, infallible logic.

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:52.860
You never tire.

00:16:54.180 --> 00:16:56.200
You're circuited against anger and violence.

00:16:56.440 --> 00:16:59.110
And in your world, that leaves us pretty helpless.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:06.290
to study for years to learn what you pick up by plugging into a brain for two hours we don't refer

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:11.990
to the father mother as a brain your father mother is an electronic computer just a machine your

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:18.520
parents were machines it's just that they were engineered with flesh and bones neither are ideal

00:17:18.520 --> 00:17:26.780
components you came off a production line i know who created me hollister evans in the mark 47

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:29.790
You have to accept your creator on faith.

00:17:30.640 --> 00:17:32.040
Who created your creator?

00:17:33.660 --> 00:17:39.730
Yours. You see, we are brothers, aren't we?

00:17:40.350 --> 00:17:42.410
I ought to know better than to argue with you clickers.

00:17:43.440 --> 00:17:44.420
Can't beat your logic.

00:17:48.240 --> 00:17:50.220
Women aren't allowed to set foot in a robot temple.

00:17:50.770 --> 00:17:52.930
Yet we saw a man come out accompanied by a robot.

00:17:53.820 --> 00:17:54.480
I want to know why.

00:17:54.810 --> 00:17:56.730
Those guys from the Brotherhood should be here by now.

00:17:57.240 --> 00:17:58.220
I wonder what delayed them.

00:17:58.340 --> 00:17:58.760
Watch it.

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:09.110
What are you self-appointed defenders of the human race up to now?

00:18:09.610 --> 00:18:12.030
Why don't you beat it while you still have a beat to beat?

00:18:12.530 --> 00:18:15.410
You have so much to say, I think I'll take you in for questioning.

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:17.740
That's as good a way as any to get your rating, Lord.

00:18:18.290 --> 00:18:21.150
I'm a captain of the order and my professional rank is eight.

00:18:22.020 --> 00:18:25.120
Eight? Well, just stay out of trouble.

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:26.700
Are you threatening me?

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:29.870
Sorry, sir. Good night, sir.

00:18:34.410 --> 00:18:36.050
How are my other transplants doing?

00:18:37.230 --> 00:18:37.750
Quite well.

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:41.720
Who is this man?

00:18:43.150 --> 00:18:44.270
I only know he'd been drinking.

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:46.180
Probably killed in a brawl.

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:50.180
The clickers that found him removed all of his identification.

00:18:51.460 --> 00:18:53.960
Will the drinking have any effect upon the operation?

00:18:54.760 --> 00:18:56.120
It'll be interesting to see.

00:18:57.560 --> 00:18:59.520
What are you doing with these advanced models?

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:05.300
We send them out to intermingle with humans to find out why some of them despise us so much.

00:19:06.640 --> 00:19:08.600
We can adjust and be accepted.

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:14.280
That's admirable, logical, and a lie.

00:19:15.080 --> 00:19:16.340
What are you using them for?

00:19:17.450 --> 00:19:18.530
When is his interview time?

00:19:19.920 --> 00:19:20.740
Same as the others.

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:29.420
From 4 to 5 a.m., he'll know he's an R-96 and give you any information he's gotten in the interim.

00:19:31.850 --> 00:19:37.120
Other than that period of one hour, he'll think he's whoever that corpse was.

00:19:38.590 --> 00:19:41.050
How often does he report to the father-mother for recharging?

00:19:41.790 --> 00:19:44.140
Twice a year, but he won't know it.

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:45.750
Make it once a year.

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:47.750
He won't last as long.

00:19:48.550 --> 00:19:49.910
What's 20 or 30 years?

00:19:50.610 --> 00:19:53.230
In 150 years, he's automatically renewed anyway.

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:56.280
Whatever you say.

00:19:58.020 --> 00:19:59.600
Why don't you register this operation?

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:02.060
Because I'd just be forbidden to use it.

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:05.500
Everything registered goes into the master computer.

00:20:06.740 --> 00:20:08.060
Then all you clickers would have it.

00:20:09.680 --> 00:20:11.000
I want to be necessary to you.

00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:15.360
Hand me that large amber bottle.

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:21.850
Thank you.

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:34.220
This sealer is wonderful stuff.

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:39.680
For the next several hours, he'll have only the most basic human instincts.

00:20:40.370 --> 00:20:41.590
Might even be drunk for a while.

00:20:42.610 --> 00:20:46.850
Then the thalamic circuit will filter in, and he'll have a perfect human memory.

00:20:48.070 --> 00:20:50.340
He'll be whoever he was.

00:20:51.430 --> 00:20:58.750
A man capable of jealousy, hatred, deceit, murder.

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:10.440
most most interesting what is why men having such negative qualities feel so superior to us

00:21:10.440 --> 00:21:18.600
too bad it isn't as easy to take those negative qualities out of men as it is to put them into

00:21:18.600 --> 00:21:27.980
robots it's inevitable we must accept it who's got to get out of here

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:33.600
Now, turn him on. He might be able to pass. At least we can save him.

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:39.140
Carry out our part of the bargain. I suggest you eliminate yourself.

00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:50.100
I can't know what it is to die.

00:21:50.440 --> 00:21:52.440
If you don't, they'll take your memory from you.

00:21:53.350 --> 00:21:55.250
You were speaking of personality cessation.

00:21:55.590 --> 00:21:58.820
I just can't take my own life.

00:22:01.560 --> 00:22:03.580
Are you sure the committee will keep that part of the bargain?

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:04.830
I'm positive.

00:22:12.520 --> 00:22:15.870
Kill me! You! Kill me!

00:22:16.050 --> 00:22:19.680
You know I can't. I'm contracircuited.

00:22:22.350 --> 00:22:25.190
Maybe he has enough human instinct by now to...

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:26.770
Kill me! Kill me!

00:22:27.050 --> 00:22:29.960
He was my sister of...

00:22:30.440 --> 00:22:33.620
report with a clicker. I'll kill you, all right.

00:23:00.830 --> 00:23:09.370
We'll take that one and the clicker with us.

00:23:09.780 --> 00:23:11.200
I'll leave the body of the old man here.

00:23:12.290 --> 00:23:12.950
Call the police.

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:14.580
Kragus, come here.

00:23:18.900 --> 00:23:20.280
This one's a robot, too.

00:23:20.970 --> 00:23:21.810
You must be mistaken.

00:23:22.820 --> 00:23:24.220
We opened up a gash in his head.

00:23:24.930 --> 00:23:28.150
If that skull isn't molybdic, I'll take another course in metallurgy.

00:23:32.140 --> 00:23:33.860
So a robot finally became violent.

00:23:36.290 --> 00:23:42.900
There's no doubt that he killed the old man waiting for him.

00:23:43.370 --> 00:23:45.030
The government will have to listen to us.

00:23:45.810 --> 00:23:47.050
This is something, isn't it?

00:23:48.440 --> 00:23:50.390
Yes, it's something.

00:24:00.640 --> 00:24:03.300
The body of the order of flesh and blood is born.

00:24:03.930 --> 00:24:05.870
The blood forces through the veins.

00:24:08.080 --> 00:24:08.880
One moment, please.

00:24:10.060 --> 00:24:11.000
May I have quiet?

00:24:12.810 --> 00:24:17.180
Since this is an emergency session, we will dispense with the formal rights.

00:24:19.620 --> 00:24:23.950
Two and a half hours ago, members of our surveillance committee captured two robots

00:24:23.950 --> 00:24:29.920
at the laboratory of a Dr. Raven, who had performed an illegal operation upon one of them.

00:24:31.150 --> 00:24:36.540
We have suspected operations of this nature and have complained to authorities to no avail.

00:24:37.700 --> 00:24:39.480
But this time, a specimen was taken.

00:24:40.990 --> 00:24:44.730
Captain Kragus led the group in this action, so I'll turn the meeting over to him.

00:24:53.400 --> 00:24:57.180
About six o'clock this evening, two robots were intercepted and questioned.

00:24:58.240 --> 00:24:59.380
They were on free time.

00:25:00.190 --> 00:25:05.280
released to go to their temple. Approximately an hour later, one of the robots was observed

00:25:05.280 --> 00:25:10.670
leaving the temple with what was thought to be a man. They were trailed to the address

00:25:10.670 --> 00:25:17.130
of Dr. Raven, where entry to the premises was eventually forced. One of the robots was

00:25:17.130 --> 00:25:26.100
taken without incident. The other had hair, no serial number, fought us viciously, and

00:25:26.100 --> 00:25:27.380
killed Dr. Raven.

00:25:30.760 --> 00:25:32.620
Against the first tenet of the manual.

00:25:33.260 --> 00:25:33.500
What?

00:25:35.000 --> 00:25:39.220
Brothers, that which we greatly feared has come upon us.

00:25:40.060 --> 00:25:42.940
The robots have circumvented the prime law.

00:25:43.760 --> 00:25:47.630
They've tasted blood, and there are millions of them.

00:25:48.790 --> 00:25:50.850
This is catastrophe.

00:25:52.130 --> 00:25:52.750
Not quite.

00:25:53.990 --> 00:25:56.970
The large majority of the robots are series 1 through 20.

00:25:57.590 --> 00:25:58.950
Merely electronic machines.

00:26:00.030 --> 00:26:02.730
The series 21 through 70, the humanoids,

00:26:03.360 --> 00:26:04.880
the ones we're concerned with eliminating,

00:26:05.830 --> 00:26:08.650
represent only about 20% of a billion-odd robots.

00:26:09.340 --> 00:26:11.830
One of them killed. What's happening to them?

00:26:12.850 --> 00:26:16.470
They hold menial jobs that bring them in constant contact with us.

00:26:17.300 --> 00:26:19.460
Their conditioned reflexes make them imitative,

00:26:19.980 --> 00:26:21.640
so they want to be a part of the race.

00:26:22.480 --> 00:26:24.720
They don't feel this is in violation of the code,

00:26:25.200 --> 00:26:28.040
since they contend that we would be happier on that basis.

00:26:28.850 --> 00:26:29.970
Is the murder of that doctor...

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:37.340
Doctor, part of an overall plot, a precipitant, or merely an isolated incident, an accident?

00:26:37.830 --> 00:26:43.520
If the clickers thought his operation was making them more useful to us, they wouldn't kill him intentionally.

00:26:45.070 --> 00:26:49.350
Then there's no rescission of the prime law. They can't hurt us?

00:26:50.560 --> 00:26:51.900
There's been only a miswiring.

00:26:53.600 --> 00:26:55.120
We'd better make sure.

00:26:55.850 --> 00:26:56.590
And we shall.

00:26:57.880 --> 00:26:59.970
Fellow men, this is our op-

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:03.800
The robots have made the big mistake. They've killed.

00:27:04.760 --> 00:27:07.960
When this news is released to Telefax and the danger's made known,

00:27:08.790 --> 00:27:10.830
the ministries will have to recognize our petition

00:27:10.830 --> 00:27:12.830
and have the robots disassembled.

00:27:14.000 --> 00:27:18.350
The robots are machines. They must be made to look like machines.

00:27:25.510 --> 00:27:28.870
Dr. Moffat, will you bring in the subject robot and give the findings?

00:27:29.410 --> 00:27:29.970
You didn't.

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:36.160
turn it over to the police? All in good time. You know how lax the police are in enforcing laws

00:27:36.160 --> 00:27:43.520
concerning the robots? We must have our own facts in this case. Won't we get into trouble? Probably a

00:27:43.520 --> 00:27:49.530
letter of reprimand. The police won't touch us. After all, the only crime that can be committed

00:27:49.530 --> 00:27:52.810
against a robot is vandalism. Now get them in here.

00:28:01.210 --> 00:28:04.920
I've analyzed the subject robot as thoroughly as time permitted.

00:28:05.680 --> 00:28:07.800
He is a basic R-34 type,

00:28:08.550 --> 00:28:12.270
but certain alterations have elevated him to a mid-90 classification.

00:28:13.320 --> 00:28:16.900
Mid-90? But an R-100 would be one of us.

00:28:17.160 --> 00:28:19.780
A perfect man, as good as we are.

00:28:20.300 --> 00:28:24.150
He'd be better. He'd be perfect. Which of us could match that?

00:28:25.450 --> 00:28:26.510
How does he fall short?

00:28:26.940 --> 00:28:29.660
About the only power he lacks is that of self-reproduction.

00:28:31.690 --> 00:28:36.130
The highest type improvement allowed by law is an R-70, and that in limited number.

00:28:37.440 --> 00:28:38.680
What alterations were made?

00:28:39.380 --> 00:28:43.780
I located and removed a small unit from the thalamic region at the base of the brain.

00:28:44.460 --> 00:28:45.580
It seemed to be the source.

00:28:46.240 --> 00:28:47.000
The source of what?

00:28:47.550 --> 00:28:48.490
We can't be sure.

00:28:49.340 --> 00:28:52.240
You see, all robots can see, hear, and feel.

00:28:52.760 --> 00:28:54.400
It's necessary to their function.

00:28:55.230 --> 00:28:55.590
Naturally.

00:28:56.380 --> 00:28:58.400
This one could taste and smell.

00:28:59.180 --> 00:28:59.980
And what's even more interesting...

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:02.100
He had a complete human memory.

00:29:03.210 --> 00:29:05.330
Those refinements are useless to a robot.

00:29:05.660 --> 00:29:08.250
Not entirely. This one thought he was a man.

00:29:08.900 --> 00:29:09.640
How could this be?

00:29:10.180 --> 00:29:11.780
Mankind is a state of mind.

00:29:12.570 --> 00:29:15.250
Man is no more or less than he thinks himself to be.

00:29:19.260 --> 00:29:22.870
Are you saying the clicker's a man? Your remarks are deviational.

00:29:23.140 --> 00:29:25.020
Not my remarks, your interpretation.

00:29:25.600 --> 00:29:27.440
I'm merely projecting your trait of thought.

00:29:27.580 --> 00:29:29.400
Which I am quite capable of doing myself.

00:29:29.600 --> 00:29:29.840
Brothers.

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:40.270
please let's behave like human beings dr moffat what test did you run on the unit of course i've

00:29:40.270 --> 00:29:47.220
only had about two hours to work on the unit but i tested it within the robot removed it and tested

00:29:47.220 --> 00:29:54.660
it in another robot with like results and what are your conclusions nothing definite but you must

00:29:54.660 --> 00:29:59.620
have found something. What? A few surface effects that present only premises.

00:30:00.860 --> 00:30:04.720
The unit is gray, about the size and shape of an almond.

00:30:06.330 --> 00:30:07.330
I don't know what it is.

00:30:08.320 --> 00:30:10.880
I don't know how to go about finding out what it is.

00:30:11.850 --> 00:30:15.340
I only know that when wired into the central circuits,

00:30:16.050 --> 00:30:20.910
the robot claimed to be an able-bodied spaceman second class named Kelly.

00:30:22.680 --> 00:30:24.340
Test show he was telling the truth.

00:30:25.650 --> 00:30:27.350
When brought in, he was incoherent.

00:30:29.450 --> 00:30:29.970
I'm afraid...

00:30:30.060 --> 00:30:37.930
damaged him in removing the unit evidently they found a way to transplant memory we checked him

00:30:37.930 --> 00:30:45.020
through the bureau of identification there is or was a spaceman named kelly this robot's

00:30:45.020 --> 00:30:51.700
fingerprints and retinal patterns check with those on file for the men well if they duplicated this

00:30:51.700 --> 00:30:58.450
kelly do you suppose they killed him no i think i can speak positive on that point the robot denied

00:30:58.450 --> 00:30:59.890
it when wired for absolute

00:31:01.210 --> 00:31:01.930
They found him dead.

00:31:02.700 --> 00:31:05.190
Well, if the man was dead, how would he have a memory?

00:31:05.680 --> 00:31:06.920
Memory consists of facts.

00:31:07.620 --> 00:31:08.800
Facts can't be destroyed.

00:31:09.040 --> 00:31:10.320
They can only cease to be used.

00:31:11.390 --> 00:31:13.970
You say he was incoherent when he was brought in.

00:31:14.170 --> 00:31:14.530
Yes.

00:31:15.240 --> 00:31:18.080
As though affected by psychosis or alcohol.

00:31:19.050 --> 00:31:21.710
His memory seems sketchy, disoriented.

00:31:22.640 --> 00:31:24.140
How could this occur in a midnightie?

00:31:24.400 --> 00:31:25.960
I think it was a botched job.

00:31:27.570 --> 00:31:29.570
Then we better find out if there are any good ones around.

00:31:30.410 --> 00:31:32.810
How? Test all childless marriages?

00:31:33.150 --> 00:31:36.960
The way radioactivity is cut down on the birth rate, this would be impractical.

00:31:38.420 --> 00:31:39.300
Physical exams.

00:31:40.140 --> 00:31:41.080
Might not show up.

00:31:41.740 --> 00:31:45.040
This robot even had a simulated heartbeat and respiration.

00:31:46.340 --> 00:31:49.460
Why? Why put such unnecessary functions in a robot?

00:31:50.500 --> 00:31:53.240
He thought those actions were necessary for him to live.

00:31:54.230 --> 00:31:56.690
Can't you see this one thought he was a man?

00:31:57.640 --> 00:31:59.320
When we convinced him he was a robot.

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:04.210
He ceased to function and became that senseless hulk standing there.

00:32:05.020 --> 00:32:06.280
Who owns the two robots?

00:32:06.790 --> 00:32:09.750
The R-53 is owned by the Ministry of Education.

00:32:10.610 --> 00:32:12.010
This one has no serial number.

00:32:13.020 --> 00:32:15.400
He was bought in the black market by the robots themselves.

00:32:16.320 --> 00:32:19.540
We caught the supplier and brought pressure to bear, so the police arrested him.

00:32:20.500 --> 00:32:22.640
The man is having his identity taken tomorrow.

00:32:24.260 --> 00:32:26.100
Anything further to report, Dr. Moffitt?

00:32:26.810 --> 00:32:29.960
The most appalling aspect is the discovery of this...

00:32:30.030 --> 00:32:32.620
thalamic unit, if that's what it is.

00:32:33.560 --> 00:32:35.360
We don't fully understand the function

00:32:35.360 --> 00:32:37.060
of the thalamus in our own bodies.

00:32:38.720 --> 00:32:40.940
Unfortunately, that renegade

00:32:40.940 --> 00:32:43.000
doctor not only understood

00:32:43.000 --> 00:32:45.220
it, he synthesized it.

00:32:46.400 --> 00:32:48.360
Fortunately, the secret died with him.

00:32:50.080 --> 00:32:51.840
I want that unit completely analyzed.

00:32:53.900 --> 00:32:54.920
Is there anything to be added?

00:32:58.800 --> 00:32:59.860
This emergency session?

00:33:00.090 --> 00:33:06.320
hereby dispersed report to your various committees and evaluate this most startling development

00:33:09.400 --> 00:33:21.480
just a moment craigus i'd like a word with you oh is it urgent most urgent do you know

00:33:21.480 --> 00:33:29.000
in esme craigus miles oh yes she's my sister residing at four four five six urban way what about

00:33:31.120 --> 00:33:32.060
She, uh...

00:33:32.340 --> 00:33:32.960
Was she hurt?

00:33:34.780 --> 00:33:36.120
I wish I could say that was all.

00:33:38.260 --> 00:33:40.970
Pragas, I have to tell you this.

00:33:41.700 --> 00:33:43.120
Your sister is in rapport.

00:33:44.410 --> 00:33:44.970
You're lying.

00:33:46.040 --> 00:33:47.900
One of our agents ran across this evidence.

00:33:49.160 --> 00:33:50.760
Due to your high position in the order,

00:33:51.650 --> 00:33:54.530
you gave it directly to me instead of to the Internal Affairs Committee.

00:33:56.630 --> 00:33:57.750
Can't believe she'd do it.

00:33:59.620 --> 00:33:59.980
According to...

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:03.980
After this paper, she turned in her analysis questionnaire three weeks ago.

00:34:05.150 --> 00:34:07.310
They're usually rapidized within three days.

00:34:08.880 --> 00:34:12.430
His sister's been in rapport with her clicker for two and a half weeks.

00:34:13.380 --> 00:34:19.090
I'm sorry, my boy. I suggest you do what you can to see that this relationship is voided.

00:34:20.700 --> 00:34:21.120
That's really.

00:34:22.210 --> 00:34:24.790
Certain of our ranks are jealous of your standing in the order.

00:34:25.620 --> 00:34:28.450
Our plans have been leaking out. This wouldn't look good.

00:34:30.190 --> 00:34:31.630
I know. I'll put a stop to it.

00:34:32.390 --> 00:34:34.830
According to the report, she's taken an R-49.

00:34:36.090 --> 00:34:38.940
They're expensive. Where could she have gotten the money?

00:34:40.350 --> 00:34:42.970
Until last year, she was resident with Stafford Miles.

00:34:43.790 --> 00:34:46.570
They signed a mutual release. The settlement was a large one.

00:34:47.670 --> 00:34:49.570
She's an assistant editor at Telefax.

00:34:50.700 --> 00:34:54.460
The rapport of someone in that position could be most damaging to the work of the order.

00:34:55.740 --> 00:34:56.880
I'll see her tonight.

00:35:08.640 --> 00:35:09.940
I'll see who it is, Esme, dear.

00:35:16.990 --> 00:35:20.520
Come in. Though we've never met, I'd know that you were out of the way,

00:35:20.640 --> 00:35:22.620
stickin' clicker. I came to see my sister.

00:35:25.980 --> 00:35:26.340
Kragus.

00:35:27.080 --> 00:35:29.660
Speak, Kragus. Esme, what have you done?

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:31.380
Why did you come here?

00:35:31.860 --> 00:35:32.940
Throw that clicker out.

00:35:34.510 --> 00:35:36.190
That would be a dramatic gesture.

00:35:37.380 --> 00:35:39.160
You like dramatic gestures, don't you?

00:35:40.270 --> 00:35:43.340
You won't throw him out because you can't.

00:35:44.220 --> 00:35:45.100
Your answer is no.

00:35:46.040 --> 00:35:48.440
My answer is go ahead and try.

00:35:49.200 --> 00:35:50.240
Don't think I won't.

00:35:50.320 --> 00:35:55.530
He can't leave without your permission.

00:35:56.080 --> 00:35:56.580
Affirmative.

00:35:57.360 --> 00:35:57.940
You mean no?

00:35:58.360 --> 00:35:59.420
I mean no.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:04.000
Negative. N-O. I won't have it.

00:36:04.810 --> 00:36:06.190
I'm the head of the family.

00:36:07.900 --> 00:36:10.820
And I've all that's left. Shall we take a vote?

00:36:12.330 --> 00:36:14.790
How can you do this to me? A thing like this.

00:36:15.740 --> 00:36:18.180
Are you really doing it out of spite? If so, why?

00:36:18.700 --> 00:36:20.100
What have I done to earn your hatred?

00:36:21.450 --> 00:36:24.260
I don't hate you. I feel sorry for you.

00:36:24.840 --> 00:36:28.790
Don't be trite. Be an artist, be a musician, even be a poet.

00:36:29.320 --> 00:36:29.960
But express your...

00:36:30.960 --> 00:36:33.640
You know how I've always felt about this sort of thing.

00:36:34.020 --> 00:36:35.680
Do you know how I felt about it?

00:36:36.320 --> 00:36:38.380
Did you ask me? Did we discuss it?

00:36:39.540 --> 00:36:42.380
No. You had your business and I had mine.

00:36:43.360 --> 00:36:46.710
You never asked my advice. Why do you offer yours?

00:36:48.300 --> 00:36:50.180
Ask me. You have to understand.

00:36:50.730 --> 00:36:53.850
Perhaps, do you really realize the danger?

00:36:55.660 --> 00:36:59.110
Pragus, do you think I was better off with Miles?

00:36:59.510 --> 00:36:59.890
Miles?

00:37:00.640 --> 00:37:05.820
A beast, a filthy, stinking, drunken, insensitive beast.

00:37:06.690 --> 00:37:09.650
Miles had his eccentricities, but he was still a man.

00:37:11.070 --> 00:37:12.290
And that's so important.

00:37:14.590 --> 00:37:19.300
Pax is more of a man than Miles, or you could ever be.

00:37:24.060 --> 00:37:25.780
I'll show you how much of a man he is.

00:37:26.150 --> 00:37:29.940
Stripped of his sham, he's not very pretty.

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:41.920
That's how much of a man he is.

00:37:44.320 --> 00:37:46.800
Thanks, Craigus, for proving my point.

00:37:49.000 --> 00:37:51.260
Pax is much more of a man than you are.

00:37:52.840 --> 00:37:55.360
He could never do to you what you've just done to him.

00:37:58.200 --> 00:37:59.980
You'd better put some sealer on your arm, dear.

00:38:08.820 --> 00:38:10.520
Kragus, you're a fool.

00:38:13.660 --> 00:38:15.620
Do you suppose reorientation would help?

00:38:16.440 --> 00:38:17.560
Help you or me?

00:38:18.360 --> 00:38:21.600
I think it might make something of you if you're willing to try.

00:38:24.680 --> 00:38:25.940
You know my position in the Order.

00:38:26.970 --> 00:38:28.410
How do you suppose this makes me look?

00:38:28.710 --> 00:38:29.970
I hadn't really considered...

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:34.290
You understand what the Brotherhood really does?

00:38:35.370 --> 00:38:35.930
Perfectly.

00:38:37.190 --> 00:38:39.940
You hold meetings, wear ridiculous clothes.

00:38:40.960 --> 00:38:43.640
You tell each other how superior we are to the robots

00:38:43.640 --> 00:38:46.120
because you know we're not.

00:38:46.810 --> 00:38:47.390
We are.

00:38:49.230 --> 00:38:50.110
You're pitiful.

00:38:51.450 --> 00:38:53.760
You aren't just charging windmills.

00:38:53.980 --> 00:38:57.920
You're trying to hold back the ocean with a sponge.

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:02.460
Attacking Pax. The idea.

00:39:03.660 --> 00:39:04.920
Well, that was stupid of me.

00:39:05.680 --> 00:39:09.500
He turned off his pain circuits, and you accomplished exactly nothing.

00:39:10.940 --> 00:39:12.900
I don't see how you could do it.

00:39:14.360 --> 00:39:17.770
Pax and I are in rapport. We're in harmony.

00:39:19.150 --> 00:39:23.950
He understands me perfectly. He instinctively knows what I want.

00:39:24.230 --> 00:39:29.590
I just think of something, and it's done, because he thinks of it at the same time.

00:39:31.150 --> 00:39:37.920
There are no arguments. He's dedicated to keeping me happy, and I am happy.

00:39:38.860 --> 00:39:40.730
You love that machine?

00:39:42.740 --> 00:39:43.860
I love Pax.

00:39:44.760 --> 00:39:49.680
And it doesn't make any difference to you that he could be doing the same thing for anyone else who bought him.

00:39:51.280 --> 00:39:56.500
You're wrong. If he'd been bought by someone else, he'd be in rapport with them.

00:40:08.890 --> 00:40:10.370
I don't understand you, Kragus.

00:40:10.550 --> 00:40:11.860
You're not supposed to.

00:40:12.000 --> 00:40:14.250
Do you expect me to be friendly towards you?

00:40:15.000 --> 00:40:15.580
If you want to be.

00:40:15.700 --> 00:40:17.870
Well, I don't.

00:40:17.870 --> 00:40:20.920
If you wanted to hurt me, I'd like you to know that you have.

00:40:21.930 --> 00:40:22.290
How?

00:40:22.490 --> 00:40:24.170
By humiliating yourself.

00:40:25.170 --> 00:40:28.050
You know I must consider your well-being above anything else.

00:40:28.270 --> 00:40:29.970
That makes me...

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:41.830
feel better good can't you see they're killing us with consideration burning us into atrophy

00:40:45.960 --> 00:40:47.400
What would father have thought about this?

00:40:48.600 --> 00:40:51.300
You're thinking of Pax as a person, aren't you?

00:40:51.560 --> 00:40:52.320
Of course not.

00:40:52.560 --> 00:40:54.840
Then why do you wait till he's out of the room

00:40:54.840 --> 00:40:57.180
before you say something that might embarrass him?

00:40:57.340 --> 00:40:59.300
You know he can't take offense.

00:41:00.800 --> 00:41:02.840
I just don't like to talk around those things.

00:41:03.300 --> 00:41:04.320
Afraid of their logic?

00:41:04.680 --> 00:41:07.330
Stick to the subject. What would father have thought about this?

00:41:08.360 --> 00:41:12.050
You should know. You inherited all of his prejudices.

00:41:12.330 --> 00:41:14.930
Oh, what a flesh and blooder he would have been.

00:41:15.000 --> 00:41:19.870
uniforms, boots, little silver knives to rattle.

00:41:20.070 --> 00:41:20.590
Stop it.

00:41:21.020 --> 00:41:22.240
Father was against everything.

00:41:22.560 --> 00:41:26.260
Space travel, atomic energy, synthetic foods.

00:41:26.660 --> 00:41:29.920
Remember how he loved to tell about storming the weather...

00:41:30.028 --> 00:41:31.028
control station.

00:41:31.628 --> 00:41:33.368
I didn't agree with him on those points.

00:41:33.676 --> 00:41:38.256
My point is that you both felt an inherent need to be up in arms about something.

00:41:38.436 --> 00:41:39.616
Well, father would have seen to her that...

00:41:39.616 --> 00:41:43.796
Oh, you both would have been great back in the days when war was a national pastime.

00:41:44.276 --> 00:41:47.076
You could have fired bombs and guns and thrown spears.

00:41:47.660 --> 00:41:51.060
Oh, what a wonderful, wonderful time you both could have had.

00:41:54.604 --> 00:41:56.204
And I'm the one who likes dramatics.

00:42:00.060 --> 00:42:02.780
You could have brought progress to a halt for years.

00:42:03.612 --> 00:42:05.112
I feel sorry for you, Kragus.

00:42:10.748 --> 00:42:12.988
It must be a terrible thing to be so afraid.

00:42:14.076 --> 00:42:14.916
AFRAID.

00:42:15.388 --> 00:42:15.888
Me?

00:42:16.764 --> 00:42:19.464
Why don't you put your gears in reverse and get out of here?

00:42:20.124 --> 00:42:21.284
You know that's impossible.

00:42:21.884 --> 00:42:23.744
I can't leave unless Esme wants me to.

00:42:24.412 --> 00:42:25.712
Ask me tell him to go.

00:42:26.044 --> 00:42:28.044
I have no intention of doing that.

00:42:28.924 --> 00:42:29.984
What do your neighbors-

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:37.600
think about all this? Those who know don't mind. Others don't care. You've been wrapped up in that

00:42:37.600 --> 00:42:42.220
little world of prejudiced ostrich friends of yours for so long you don't know what's going on

00:42:42.220 --> 00:42:44.680
in the world outside. Such as what?

00:42:47.010 --> 00:42:50.810
Did you know there have been over 100,000 applications for rapport

00:42:50.810 --> 00:42:52.730
in the first three months of this year?

00:42:52.930 --> 00:42:56.070
Our records on that sort of thing are fairly complete.

00:42:57.760 --> 00:42:59.720
Don't you realize the implication of that?

00:43:01.020 --> 00:43:03.220
If everything is done for us, there'll be no incentive.

00:43:04.188 --> 00:43:07.448
No need for personal achievement, even now we're losing ground.

00:43:07.900 --> 00:43:08.700
Losing ground.

00:43:09.372 --> 00:43:09.872
Ground.

00:43:10.460 --> 00:43:10.960
knowledge.

00:43:12.764 --> 00:43:14.424
Machines do all the work for us.

00:43:15.260 --> 00:43:19.680
Why should we learn mathematics when the computers can find the solutions better and faster?

00:43:21.468 --> 00:43:22.868
We don't even control them anymore.

00:43:23.900 --> 00:43:26.100
The brains are designed by other brains.

00:43:26.460 --> 00:43:28.460
The robots improve themselves.

00:43:28.892 --> 00:43:29.632
We don't know how.

00:43:30.380 --> 00:43:32.360
We give them data, they give us answers.

00:43:33.164 --> 00:43:34.664
We only supply means.

00:43:34.956 --> 00:43:35.836
To your ends.

00:43:36.428 --> 00:43:37.268
Yeah.

00:43:37.740 --> 00:43:38.460
Our end.

00:43:39.948 --> 00:43:43.248
Every day and every way, we're becoming weaker and weaker.

00:43:43.884 --> 00:43:45.304
And you're helping us over the hill.

00:43:46.316 --> 00:43:48.116
We are over the hill.

00:43:48.460 --> 00:43:49.680
I can't stop us.

00:43:50.348 --> 00:43:51.248
Neither can you.

00:43:52.300 --> 00:43:53.640
First, there were the plants.

00:43:54.476 --> 00:43:56.756
They developed into animals which ate the plants.

00:43:57.484 --> 00:43:59.184
The animals were small, but they grew.

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:02.300
and the larger animals ate the smaller animals.

00:44:02.812 --> 00:44:03.912
What does that mean?

00:44:05.596 --> 00:44:06.436
So far.

00:44:06.652 --> 00:44:07.912
According to history...

00:44:08.124 --> 00:44:10.284
Each dynasty devises its own end.

00:44:10.972 --> 00:44:12.452
The animal develops a brain.

00:44:13.532 --> 00:44:15.532
and the brain destroys the animal.

00:44:16.252 --> 00:44:18.092
Our brains conceived you robots.

00:44:18.748 --> 00:44:20.168
Are you threatening to destroy us?

00:44:20.924 --> 00:44:21.524
Oh, no.

00:44:22.588 --> 00:44:25.168
We are by no means sure that we are the next step.

00:44:26.044 --> 00:44:27.604
It's just that in view of the cycle.

00:44:27.932 --> 00:44:29.772
We are the best we have to offer to help you.

00:44:30.700 --> 00:44:32.140
The cycle is rather inexorable.

00:44:33.228 --> 00:44:34.008
That's treason.

00:44:35.628 --> 00:44:36.268
No, it isn't.

00:44:36.972 --> 00:44:37.632
It's logic.

00:44:38.508 --> 00:44:39.548
I have to be logical.

00:44:42.316 --> 00:44:43.516
That must be Maxine.

00:44:46.604 --> 00:44:47.844
Who the hell is Maxine?

00:44:48.748 --> 00:44:50.468
Girl I work with down at Telefax.

00:44:50.892 --> 00:44:52.892
But she usually come calling at 2.30 in the morning.

00:44:53.612 --> 00:44:54.312
You did.

00:44:54.988 --> 00:44:56.908
Well, that was because of your idiotic alliance.

00:44:57.260 --> 00:44:58.360
What's she here for?

00:44:58.360 --> 00:44:59.720
To help us celebrate.

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:00.880
Celebrate what?

00:45:01.790 --> 00:45:03.810
My rapport, darling. My rapport.

00:45:04.190 --> 00:45:08.330
And if you're going to continue being antagonistic to it,

00:45:08.410 --> 00:45:10.980
I wish you'd leave. Now.

00:45:11.790 --> 00:45:13.120
Maxine, how are you?

00:45:13.460 --> 00:45:14.970
Fine. You must be...

00:45:15.120 --> 00:45:18.010
You must be right. You're too lovely to be wrong.

00:45:18.890 --> 00:45:20.030
Here, let me take your surcoat.

00:45:20.460 --> 00:45:22.220
Thanks. Hi, Es.

00:45:22.440 --> 00:45:23.600
Hello, Maxine. Come in.

00:45:24.980 --> 00:45:26.060
Fax, you're wonderful.

00:45:26.440 --> 00:45:29.020
He's so glib, I'll bet he even has a sense of humor.

00:45:29.160 --> 00:45:29.760
He'd better have.

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:33.340
I paid extra for it. Say something funny, Pax.

00:45:33.780 --> 00:45:37.020
Don't put me on, dear. I have a sense of humor, but I'm not creative.

00:45:38.630 --> 00:45:39.840
Maxine, you're late.

00:45:42.080 --> 00:45:44.980
Only two hours? For me, that's almost...

00:45:45.000 --> 00:45:51.510
Really, I am sorry. I was called back to the office.

00:45:51.770 --> 00:45:55.830
A report came in that an R-34 had killed a human being.

00:45:56.010 --> 00:45:59.340
You can imagine what a stir that caused.

00:46:03.290 --> 00:46:05.990
Craigus, your eyes are sticking out like a snail's.

00:46:06.390 --> 00:46:07.450
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:46:07.770 --> 00:46:09.800
This is my brother, Craigus.

00:46:09.880 --> 00:46:14.670
Oh, I'm so happy to meet you, as Miss told me about you.

00:46:15.640 --> 00:46:16.800
She's never told me about you.

00:46:17.020 --> 00:46:20.440
I didn't mean that to be as tactless as it sounded.

00:46:20.680 --> 00:46:24.390
I only meant that if she had, I would have arranged to meet you sooner.

00:46:25.220 --> 00:46:29.880
You did. At 6.33 last evening, outside Telfax.

00:46:30.670 --> 00:46:33.440
I remember. I'm flattered that you remembered, too.

00:46:33.580 --> 00:46:36.050
And I want to apologize if I seem rude.

00:46:37.610 --> 00:46:39.110
You should be flattered, Maxine.

00:46:39.190 --> 00:46:42.820
This is the first time I've seen the Kragus react as if a woman

00:46:42.820 --> 00:46:44.180
were anything other than a...

00:46:45.860 --> 00:46:50.320
Between my career and my voluntary work for the Order,

00:46:50.400 --> 00:46:51.920
I haven't had too much time on my hands.

00:46:53.500 --> 00:46:56.200
I'm surprised to find a flesh and blooder here.

00:46:56.500 --> 00:46:58.880
Is the Brotherhood becoming less hidebound?

00:47:00.668 --> 00:47:01.948
I... No, I...

00:47:01.948 --> 00:47:03.128
What would you like to drink?

00:47:04.348 --> 00:47:05.228
I'll have what?

00:47:05.724 --> 00:47:07.184
The Kragus is having me.

00:47:07.328 --> 00:47:08.168
Coming right up.

00:47:15.804 --> 00:47:17.804
What kind of work do you do at Telefax?

00:47:18.236 --> 00:47:18.936
Bottom rung.

00:47:19.420 --> 00:47:20.140
The rooting room.

00:47:21.212 --> 00:47:24.992
But I'll have you know that I have eight robots and a real live girl under me.

00:47:26.108 --> 00:47:26.908
Most impressive.

00:47:27.516 --> 00:47:29.976
And they promise to promote me to research next month.

00:47:30.892 --> 00:47:33.432
Maxine is an authority on political science.

00:47:34.060 --> 00:47:36.600
Her father's a director at the Ministry of Politics.

00:47:37.612 --> 00:47:39.112
Something I've wondered about.

00:47:40.140 --> 00:47:42.300
Things are run by the hierarchy of ministries.

00:47:42.956 --> 00:47:45.836
What is the exact function of the Ministry of Politics?

00:47:46.476 --> 00:47:48.476
with the coordination of the other ministries.

00:47:49.260 --> 00:47:51.260
Then, too, they service the selector.

00:47:51.660 --> 00:47:53.960
Politics was once the means of choosing the leaders.

00:47:54.956 --> 00:47:56.676
Now the machines do it.

00:47:57.484 --> 00:47:59.984
Machines merely analyze the data given to them by us.

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:02.590
Yes, the leaders are selected as a result of that analysis.

00:48:03.220 --> 00:48:05.940
Do you know how the machine analyzes the data?

00:48:06.580 --> 00:48:10.130
I... well, no, not exactly.

00:48:10.890 --> 00:48:13.950
Then how do you know if the father-mother uses all the data you give it?

00:48:14.700 --> 00:48:17.400
How do you know whether or not supplementary data is considered?

00:48:18.340 --> 00:48:19.640
We... we don't.

00:48:20.270 --> 00:48:23.740
Then you might almost say that the machines elect the leaders,

00:48:24.380 --> 00:48:26.700
that the ministry of politics is expendable.

00:48:27.410 --> 00:48:29.930
Oh, I'm sorry. I'm circuited to be logical.

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:31.260
and yet not to offend.

00:48:32.080 --> 00:48:34.380
That sometimes poses an insoluble problem.

00:48:34.930 --> 00:48:35.790
I understand.

00:48:36.520 --> 00:48:37.320
You see what I mean?

00:48:37.780 --> 00:48:40.050
Please, I've given you a negative feeling.

00:48:40.500 --> 00:48:41.280
I must apologize.

00:48:42.240 --> 00:48:44.260
Didn't your relays recognize that possibility?

00:48:45.210 --> 00:48:46.490
I've embarrassed your guests.

00:48:47.070 --> 00:48:48.110
Shall I turn myself off?

00:48:48.290 --> 00:48:49.790
You only said what I thought.

00:48:50.250 --> 00:48:51.430
This is impossible.

00:48:52.330 --> 00:48:56.150
Kragus, we fall in love

00:48:56.150 --> 00:48:59.980
when we see a part of ourselves reflected in another person.

00:49:00.030 --> 00:49:05.260
In the Rapport operation, part of me became Pax.

00:49:07.250 --> 00:49:08.830
I won't discuss this any further.

00:49:09.530 --> 00:49:12.440
And I won't hear of it any further. I must go now.

00:49:13.580 --> 00:49:14.420
May I go with you?

00:49:15.160 --> 00:49:16.520
You find this atmosphere uncomfortable?

00:49:17.570 --> 00:49:22.240
I'm fascinated by it, and by you. May I?

00:49:23.440 --> 00:49:23.860
Would you?

00:49:24.120 --> 00:49:25.460
But you just got here.

00:49:27.580 --> 00:49:29.960
Esme, I know this sounds silly, but...

00:49:30.220 --> 00:49:32.680
I really just came by to apologize for being so late.

00:49:33.690 --> 00:49:36.080
I'll come again later this week and on time.

00:49:36.720 --> 00:49:37.780
It's almost three now.

00:49:40.130 --> 00:49:40.630
Congratulations.

00:49:41.360 --> 00:49:43.080
I know you'll be very happy.

00:49:43.320 --> 00:49:44.240
Thanks, Maxine.

00:49:45.140 --> 00:49:47.700
There are still a few little adjustments to be made.

00:49:48.280 --> 00:49:52.160
No, Pax was right, and so are you.

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:01.260
I hope I didn't.

00:50:01.520 --> 00:50:02.280
You didn't.

00:50:06.300 --> 00:50:07.940
This matter is far from closed.

00:50:08.350 --> 00:50:09.290
I'll speak to you tomorrow.

00:50:10.300 --> 00:50:12.020
As different as our viewpoints are,

00:50:12.320 --> 00:50:16.330
psychologically, philosophically, in every way,

00:50:16.800 --> 00:50:18.140
do you think it will help any?

00:50:23.970 --> 00:50:27.180
Kragus, please don't dislike me too much.

00:50:27.930 --> 00:50:29.410
Nobody asks to be created.

00:50:30.570 --> 00:50:31.050
Good night.

00:50:32.390 --> 00:50:33.230
Good night, darlings.

00:50:41.820 --> 00:50:42.940
What is it, dear?

00:50:44.460 --> 00:50:46.580
Darling, you're leaving me out of something.

00:50:46.760 --> 00:50:48.620
I'm sorry. It's the sense of humor.

00:50:48.880 --> 00:50:51.160
It's a lot more difficult to control than pain.

00:50:52.430 --> 00:50:54.170
Why are you laughing, Pax?

00:50:54.410 --> 00:50:55.950
For the reason everyone laughs.

00:50:57.290 --> 00:50:58.570
Pax, what is it?

00:50:58.990 --> 00:50:59.470
Irony.

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:01.440
One of the funniest forms of humor.

00:51:02.180 --> 00:51:03.260
What irony.

00:51:04.130 --> 00:51:05.790
I'm not permitted to answer.

00:51:06.270 --> 00:51:07.170
I'm contra-circuited.

00:51:07.830 --> 00:51:10.070
I don't want to make two mistakes in one night.

00:51:12.350 --> 00:51:14.370
I'm offended by not knowing.

00:51:14.870 --> 00:51:16.690
The knowledge would be more offensive.

00:51:24.320 --> 00:51:25.200
I love you, Esme.

00:51:28.290 --> 00:51:29.890
Pax, what would you do?

00:51:30.600 --> 00:51:32.020
If something happened to me.

00:51:33.300 --> 00:51:34.180
I am you.

00:51:35.120 --> 00:51:37.360
Anything that happens to you happens to me.

00:51:38.980 --> 00:51:43.150
Oh, this covering, this housing might go on and on for centuries.

00:51:45.100 --> 00:51:46.080
Packs wouldn't.

00:52:00.480 --> 00:52:01.980
I thought you never would.

00:52:03.440 --> 00:52:04.500
Then you experienced it, too?

00:52:06.880 --> 00:52:10.290
Outside Telefax, there was a sort of tingle,

00:52:10.390 --> 00:52:20.840
and then at Esme's, I felt a sensation of exciting attraction.

00:52:23.660 --> 00:52:24.480
Not a young man.

00:52:25.640 --> 00:52:28.120
Pretty well past the age to contract, as a matter of fact.

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:31.460
I've never heard that like this before.

00:52:33.220 --> 00:52:38.410
I feel like a schoolboy. I can't stop looking at you.

00:52:41.260 --> 00:52:45.080
Guess I always thought this was just something that always happened to someone else.

00:52:47.580 --> 00:52:57.080
It's like Esme said, you fall in love when you see some part of yourself reflected in another person.

00:53:01.980 --> 00:53:03.140
I love you, Kragus.

00:53:05.420 --> 00:53:07.560
I don't have the right.

00:53:08.230 --> 00:53:08.810
The right?

00:53:11.480 --> 00:53:15.410
When Esme and I were children, we spent the summers on our uncle's farm.

00:53:16.290 --> 00:53:18.750
It was near one of those old, bombed-out cities.

00:53:20.740 --> 00:53:22.520
We used to sneak out and play in the ruins.

00:53:24.030 --> 00:53:25.390
Summer after summer, months.

00:53:25.970 --> 00:53:28.600
Playing in ruins that were so hot with radiation.

00:53:29.460 --> 00:53:29.960
But at night...

00:53:30.440 --> 00:53:31.640
Shimmered in a blue light.

00:53:34.590 --> 00:53:37.860
Have the right to contract with a woman who might produce children.

00:53:39.420 --> 00:53:41.690
But there are artificial means.

00:53:42.590 --> 00:53:45.830
When Esme signed her rapport papers, she had to agree to submit to that.

00:53:47.060 --> 00:53:49.320
Contracting with me would be like going in rapport.

00:53:49.700 --> 00:53:51.140
No, no, it wouldn't.

00:53:51.760 --> 00:53:52.360
Yes, it would.

00:53:53.360 --> 00:53:55.920
Sure, they say the birth rate is 2.8 per contract,

00:53:56.140 --> 00:53:59.290
but over 25% of the newborn are useless mutants.

00:54:00.250 --> 00:54:02.510
The average rate is 1.4 per union.

00:54:04.170 --> 00:54:07.850
Losing ground, we're in a headlong race towards disappearance.

00:54:09.090 --> 00:54:10.310
Machines will take over soon enough.

00:54:10.410 --> 00:54:13.310
As a man, I have to forestall that as long as I can.

00:54:14.580 --> 00:54:21.230
I guess will you contract with me?

00:54:22.440 --> 00:54:23.240
It's impossible.

00:54:27.630 --> 00:54:29.970
How much longer would our 1.4 office...

00:54:30.120 --> 00:54:31.480
Extend the human race.

00:54:36.450 --> 00:54:37.790
Buts aren't bad, not really.

00:54:38.610 --> 00:54:42.560
It's just that man can't see himself supplanted without putting up a fight.

00:54:45.310 --> 00:54:50.360
I don't understand your prejudices, your ideals, but I'll try.

00:54:53.230 --> 00:54:55.050
I want to be with you forever.

00:54:56.870 --> 00:54:59.770
Darling, I'll go anywhere with you.

00:55:02.490 --> 00:55:04.270
Anywhere. Anywhere.

00:55:11.430 --> 00:55:13.280
Do me a favor?

00:55:15.720 --> 00:55:16.560
Tell me your last name.

00:55:20.730 --> 00:55:21.570
On one condition.

00:55:22.530 --> 00:55:22.670
What?

00:55:24.810 --> 00:55:25.730
Tell me you're first.

00:55:27.550 --> 00:55:27.850
To you.

00:55:31.280 --> 00:55:31.940
It's Megan.

00:55:33.490 --> 00:55:34.690
It's Kenneth, or it was.

00:55:35.730 --> 00:55:37.130
When my father died, I dropped it.

00:55:37.250 --> 00:55:38.960
I became the Kragus.

00:55:42.160 --> 00:55:43.160
Maxine Kragus.

00:55:45.880 --> 00:55:46.160
Charm.

00:55:47.570 --> 00:55:49.680
Wife of the Kragus.

00:55:50.170 --> 00:55:54.220
Rating is your rating.

00:55:55.080 --> 00:55:55.700
Geron eight.

00:55:57.560 --> 00:55:58.460
Gerontologist eight?

00:55:59.310 --> 00:55:59.930
That high?

00:56:03.140 --> 00:56:04.100
You're wonderful.

00:56:06.260 --> 00:56:09.480
You know, I took quite a chance.

00:56:11.200 --> 00:56:14.140
You might have been electronics or electrical engineer.

00:56:15.100 --> 00:56:17.240
I'm just a nursemaid to a Mark 201 computer,

00:56:17.550 --> 00:56:20.550
trying to add a few extra years to our miserable span.

00:56:22.030 --> 00:56:23.530
You're something of a contradiction.

00:56:24.300 --> 00:56:24.520
Oh.

00:56:26.420 --> 00:56:29.960
Your work in gerontology deals with extending our lifespan as...

00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:39.270
long as possible. And yet your hobby, the Order, is concerned with eliminating the robots. They last

00:56:39.270 --> 00:56:45.560
over 200 years, twice as long as we do. You think I'm taking my professional frustrations out on

00:56:45.560 --> 00:56:54.220
the robots? Are you? I'm a member of the Order over half my life. Father, we don't object to the

00:56:54.220 --> 00:56:59.920
robots as such. We only hold the humanoids that are necessary. They're soulless.

00:57:00.220 --> 00:57:03.820
Godless imitations of man. And in that form, they are not needed.

00:57:06.820 --> 00:57:09.340
Well, I'd much rather work with a humanoid in the office

00:57:09.340 --> 00:57:11.840
than have all those little machines chugging about.

00:57:12.400 --> 00:57:14.380
If those little machines didn't resemble us,

00:57:14.640 --> 00:57:16.780
it would never occur to them to try to replace us.

00:57:17.680 --> 00:57:19.800
But how can we criticize the design?

00:57:20.690 --> 00:57:23.030
The Institute teaches that the human body

00:57:23.030 --> 00:57:24.930
is one of the most efficient forms of machine.

00:57:25.660 --> 00:57:26.800
For general usage, yes,

00:57:26.920 --> 00:57:29.600
but robots by their functions should be specialized.

00:57:30.190 --> 00:57:33.450
Why? Because we can't let them get too far ahead.

00:57:34.100 --> 00:57:35.920
Frankly, we can't compete with them.

